==============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
==============================================================================

The source tree contains no third-party code. Everything under src/, test/,
scripts/, eslint-rules/, and docs/ is original work licensed under the Apache
License 2.0; third-party packages are resolved from npm at build time and
node_modules/ is not tracked in git.

The distribution is a different matter. Couch Companion UI is a browser
application with a hard requirement that it run air-gapped, reaching no
third-party host at runtime (see vite.config.ts). Meeting that requirement
means `npm run build` copies the components below into dist/, and the release
tarball produced by scripts/package.sh wraps that same directory. Anyone
redistributing dist/ or the tarball is redistributing these components too,
and must carry the notices in this section along with them.

The full text of each license named here is appended to the LICENSE file
under "COUCH COMPANION UI SUBCOMPONENTS".

